# Every verdict in rats/out/ was produced by this binary evaluating
# rats/policy.rego. third_party/README.md's argument for pinning spdm-dump
# applies here word for word: the bytes have provenance and the reading of them
# does not, unless the reader is recorded too.
#
# rego-version= is the field that matters, and it is the only one
# harness/verify_repo.sh and harness/doctor.sh compare. OPA made Rego v1 the
# default in 1.0 and the two dialects are not compatible: DMTF's shipped
# SpdmSamplePolicy.rego is v0 and produces eleven rego_parse_error messages on
# this binary. A patch release of OPA is not a reason to fail a build; a
# different policy language is.
#
# Not vendored, and not committed. It is a 64 MB static binary belonging to
# somebody else, and the same three reasons in third_party/README.md apply. The
# CI job installs this exact version from the URL above; a workstation is
# checked against rego-version= rather than against the whole string, because a
# contributor on a distribution package should not be blocked by a build hash.
